WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.678
At agency scale, Lifecycle Workflows'
limits bite in predictable ways,

2
00:00:04.678 --> 00:00:07.550
and the responses here
are design guidance.

3
00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.666
The tenant allows a hundred
workflows; one per tree,

4
00:00:10.666 --> 00:00:14.375
event and worker type would
already need a hundred and eight.

5
00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:17.563
So build a few general
workflows that branch on codes.

6
00:00:17.563 --> 00:00:22.373
An on-demand run skips the workflow's
own conditions and its execution limits,

7
00:00:22.373 --> 00:00:25.379
so run it on the wrong
people and nothing stops it;

8
00:00:25.379 --> 00:00:28.912
treat every on-demand run as
a change with a second person.

9
00:00:28.912 --> 00:00:33.093
Execution limits quarantine a mass
event until someone approves,

10
00:00:33.093 --> 00:00:37.501
so plan a reorganization as a rehearsed
change with an agreed release.

11
00:00:37.501 --> 00:00:41.291
The kit reports late HR data that
missed the three-day catch-up,

12
00:00:41.291 --> 00:00:46.030
workflows with no execution limit, and
a warning as you approach the ceiling.
